cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Hindcast or its results, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "Hindcast: multi-agent causal simulation for strategic forecasting on time-locked evidence"
abstract: >-
  Hindcast compiles a strategic forecasting question into a typed causal graph
  of actors, objectives and world factors, simulates it with LLM agents that can
  only retrieve evidence published before the question's cutoff date, and scores
  the resulting forecast against the real resolution. Retrieval over 1,998,127
  evidence chunks is time-locked inside PostgreSQL, every model call is recorded,
  every run replays to an identical event-log hash, and the event log has a
  Terraform-managed analytics plane on AWS (S3, KMS, Glue, Athena). The
  simulation engine is distributed as the `cascade` Python package.
authors:
